module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.emitted_int_arithmetic_wraps_where_the_interpreter_refuses

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

data emitted_int_arithmetic_wraps_where_the_interpreter_refuses: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "emitted_int_arithmetic_wraps_where_the_interpreter_refuses" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "emitted Int arithmetic WRAPS where the interpreter REFUSES (one accepted program, two realizations, and on every overflowing input one of them returns a fabricated value).",

    "INVALID STATE: a substrate Int operator realized on Rust as the bare i64 infix token. The interpreter evaluates + - * / % and negation with checked arithmetic and refuses with IntegerOverflow or DivisionByZero (v1.interpreter eval_int_binop, eval_unaryop); Rust's + - * and prefix - on i64 trap only under overflow-checks, which neither the workspace release profile nor any emitted Cargo.toml turns on, so in release they wrap in two's complement -- the fact extdeps.languages.rust.primitives already recorded on the i64 row as overflow: TwoComplementWrap, and nothing consulted.",

    "HARM: silent wrongness on the source-to-Rust path, outside the DESIGN section 4b ladder. It covered every emitted crate AND the seed's own generated arithmetic: after the repair 556 operator sites across 46 stage0 mirror files route through the refusing helpers (357 add, 115 sub, 43 mul, 24 div, 10 rem, 7 neg).",

    "THE INTERPRETER'S REFUSAL IS TERMINAL, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES A PANIC THE FAITHFUL REALIZATION: an operator IntegerOverflow is an Err(InterpError) propagated by ? to a failed run; no interpreter arm converts it back into a Value a program can match. The matchable form is a different API, std.checked_arithmetic CheckedInt, whose bodies apply the operators only to operands proven in range, so it is unaffected.",

    "DISCRIMINATING RED, executed 2026-09-24 on a BuildBuddy amd64 runner, emitted crate built with cargo --release: `fn bump(x: Int) -> Int { x + 1 }` at 9223372036854775807 printed -9223372036854775808 and exited 0; sub at i64::MIN, mul at 2^62*2 and negation of i64::MIN likewise wrapped. / and % by zero and i64::MIN / -1 and i64::MIN % -1 already panicked in release, but with rustc's text rather than the interpreter's (the last as 'attempt to calculate the remainder with overflow', where the interpreter takes the % IntegerOverflow arm and NOT DivisionByZero). The interpreter refused all eight with IntegerOverflow or DivisionByZero.",

    "REPAIR: one realization authority. extdeps.languages.rust.emit rust_refusing_int_operator_helper and rust_refusing_int_negation_helper name the helpers; v1.compiler.emit_rust emit_rust_host_bin_op and emit_typed_expr route every operand whose realized checkpoint is rust_refusing_int_target_type through them; v1.compiler.runtime_rust rt_checked_int_ops realizes them with checked_* and panics with the interpreter's own Display text. GREEN, same runner and harness: all eight overflowing cases refuse with the interpreter's message, and the in-range control returns 55 on both arms.",

    "COST: the regen round (claim_executor --required-regen, whole population, one runner) measured 384819 ms on the pre-repair seed and 354101 ms on the fixed-point repaired seed; the difference is inside runner noise and is not claimed as a speedup, only as no measurable regression.",

    "RESIDUE, named so the row is not read as retired: an operand whose type realizes as some integer primitive OTHER than i64 still splices the wrapping token; the Go emitter's Int operators are unexamined against the same red; and hand-written seed Rust still wraps in release because overflow-checks is off in [profile.release] -- recommended as defense-in-depth and deliberately not flipped in this change.",

    "RUNG, STATED AT WHAT EXECUTES AND NOT AT WHAT IS WRITTEN (DESIGN section 4b(1)): MITIGATABLE today. The route is guarded by the enrolled witness test.claim.emitter_refusing_int_operator_witness_test -- the discriminating RED is the pre-repair spelling (x.clone() + 1) and friends as forbidden text, the positive control is Float keeping its infix operators -- and that witness would make the class mechanically preventable, but the whole witness population is off the required gate under the declared drop gunbc.rung_drop witness_floor_off_the_required_gate, so an emitter arm splicing an Int token directly would turn no required check red. The rung rises to mechanically preventable by THAT drop's restoration trigger and by nothing this row does.",

    "CEILING AND NEXT TRIGGER BEYOND IT, as a capability: the Int operator's overflow semantics declared once in the substrate and consulted by the interpreter and by EVERY emission target's operator realization, so a target whose primitive's overflow disagrees refuses emission rather than splicing its token -- structurally guaranteed, not merely witnessed."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.emitter_refusing_int_operator_witness_test", decl_name: "w_int_binary_operators_route_through_refusing_helpers", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.emitter_refusing_int_operator_witness_test", decl_name: "w_int_negation_routes_through_refusing_helper", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.emitter_refusing_int_operator_witness_test", decl_name: "w_float_operators_keep_infix", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
